config HERMES
	tristate "Hermes/HFA384x chipset 802.11b support (Orinoco/Prism2/Symbol)"
	depends on PCMCIA
	depends on CFG80211
	select CRYPTO
	select CRYPTO_AES
	select CRYPTO_AEAD
	select CRYPTO_CCM
	help
	  A driver for 802.11b wireless cards based on the "Hermes" or
	  Intersil HFA384x (Prism 2) MAC controller, as used in the Lucent
	  Orinoco and Cabletron RoamAbout cards and most of their rebadges.

	  This option builds the chip transport (register/command/BAP
	  access) and the bus-independent driver core (net_device plus
	  cfg80211 wiphy, nl80211-only -- no wireless-extensions ioctls).
	  It does nothing by itself without a bus client
	  (CONFIG_PCMCIA_HERMES below).

config HERMES_PRISM
	bool "Support Prism 2/2.5 chipset"
	depends on HERMES
	default y
	help
	  Say Y to enable support for Prism 2 and 2.5 chipsets.

	  Prism firmware does no WPA crypto itself; it hands the cipher to
	  the host (the HOSTENCRYPT/HOSTDECRYPT bits of CNFWEPFLAGS), so
	  the driver does WPA2/CCMP in software. This needs station
	  firmware 1.7.0 or newer, which can put the RSN element into the
	  association request it builds.

	  If you are not sure, say Y.

config HERMES_PRISM_FWDL
	bool "Volatile (RAM-only) firmware download for Prism 2/2.5"
	depends on HERMES_PRISM
	select FW_LOADER
	help
	  Say Y to let an operator load an Intersil Prism Secondary/Station
	  firmware image into the card's RAM at runtime, replacing the
	  flash-resident firmware until the next hardware-level reset
	  (power cycle, PCMCIA card/COR reset, or a suspend/resume that
	  power-cycles the socket). The Hermes INIT command the driver
	  issues afterwards is not such a reset and does not revert the
	  download. The download is triggered only by writing "1" to
	  /sys/class/net/wlanN/prism_download, never automatically at probe
	  time.

	  The image is requested as intersil/prism_sta_fw.hex. Images with
	  PDA-plug records are personalized from the card's own PDA, which
	  must be readable and CRC-clean or the download is refused.

	  If the Station image needs a PRI interface range that the
	  card's Primary firmware does not supply (a Prism 2.5 card with
	  Primary 1.0.x and a 1.7/1.8 Station image), the driver first
	  downloads a RAM Primary requested as intersil/prism_pri_fw.hex,
	  then the Station image. With no such file it refuses before
	  touching the card.

	  This only ever writes to volatile (RAM) storage: it never
	  issues the card's non-volatile/flash programming command.

	  If unsure, say N.

config PCMCIA_HERMES
	tristate "Hermes PCMCIA card support"
	depends on HERMES && PCMCIA && HAS_IOPORT_MAP
	help
	  PCMCIA/CompactFlash client glue for "Hermes" chipset based wireless
	  adaptors, such as the Lucent WavelanIEEE/Orinoco cards and their
	  OEM (Cabletron/EnteraSys RoamAbout 802.11, ELSA Airlancer, Melco
	  Buffalo and others). It should also be usable on various Prism II
	  based cards such as the Linksys, D-Link and Farallon Skyline.
